<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

<!--
  Fields:
    requiredGene    - the gene the mother must have active. Optional if sourceXenotype is set.
    sourceXenotype  - the xenotype the mother must be. Optional if requiredGene is set.
    targetXenotype  - what the baby is born as. Required.
    chance          - 0 to 1. A def with chance 1 acts as a guaranteed fallback.
    InheritanceMode - none | excess | endo | xeno | all
    order           - optional. Lower rolls first; defaults to 0.

  How multiple defs resolve:
    Every def that matches the mother is rolled in turn, lowest order first, and
    the first one to pass its chance wins. Nothing else is rolled after that. If
    every def misses, the birth falls through to the normal game behaviour.

    Defs that leave "order" unset all sit at 0 and keep their XML order, so
    listing them in the sequence you want is enough within a single file. Set
    "order" explicitly when defs come from more than one file or mod, since load
    order is not something you can rely on across files.

    A guaranteed fallback is just the last def in the sequence with chance 1:

      <order>0</order> <chance>0.05</chance>  -> tried first
      <order>1</order> <chance>0.05</chance>  -> tried if the above missed
      <order>2</order> <chance>1</chance>     -> always taken if both missed
-->

